If you have access to gopher, you can see get many historical
documents on-line. Try this command:

gopher -p"1/Ebooks/By Title/Histdocs" joeboy.micro.umn.edu

The documents (as of 1/11/93) are Amendments, Annapolis Convention,
Articles of Confederation, Bill of Rights, Charlotte Town Resolves,
Constitution, Continental Congress Resolves, Declaration of Arms,
Declaration of Independence, Emancipation Proclamation, First
Thanksgiving Proclamation, Fundamental Orders 1639, German Surrender,
Gettysburg Address, I Have a Dream, Iroquois Constitution, Iroquois
Constitution (README), Japanese Surrender, Jefferson Inaugural,
Lincoln Inaugural 2, Magna Carta, Mayflower Compact, Monroe Doctrine,
Northwest Ordinance, Paris Treaty 1783, Proclamation of Neutrality,
Rights of Man, Transmittal, Treaty of Greenville, Virginia Declaration
of Rights, Washington Farewell
